{"id":"bbb54606ab947c581dfa03fe3db1319fb03d190c156bfb49190eb7a9208f0190","lamport":0,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-10-04T12:18:03.069626Z","format_version":1,"kind":"create","payload":{"fields":{"created-at":"2026-10-04T12:18:03.069626Z","created-by":"carlo.cifarelli@gmail.com","description":"Low-risk de-risking step 1/6 of the op-log roadmap (parent 0e7b1245).\n\nDerive ids from SHA-256 of operation content (git-bug precedent) so ids need no\ncentral coordination and dedupe automatically: two clones computing the same\ncontent derive the same id. Prerequisite for the op-log flagship.","parent":"0e7b1245-e860-4843-9df3-101cd9a0a746","priority":"3","spec":"# Spec — Content-derived IDs (SHA-256 of op content)\n\nRoadmap step 1/6 (parent 0e7b12). Low-risk; prerequisite for the op-log flagship.\n\n## Goal\n\nMake operation identifiers derive deterministically from a SHA-256 hash of the\noperation's content, so two clones that independently record the same operation\ncompute the same id — no central coordination, automatic dedupe, and a stable\ntiebreaker for equal Lamport values.\n\nScope note: this step is about **operation** ids, not ticket ids. Ticket ids stay\nUUIDs (`Ticket.id: Uuid`, `Uuid::new_v4()` in `store.rs::create`); the short-id\nhandle and `resolve_id` prefix matching are unchanged and must keep working.\n\n## Current state\n\n- `store.rs::create` mints ticket ids with `Uuid::new_v4()` (random, non-derived).\n- There is no operation concept yet; this step defines the hashing primitive the\n  op-log (step 4) will consume, landed early and in isolation so step 4 does not\n  also have to bake its own id scheme.\n\n## Design\n\n- Define a canonical byte serialization for an operation payload (see step 4 for\n  the op shape). Canonical = deterministic field order + stable encoding (serde\n  with `BTreeMap`/sorted keys; no `HashMap` iteration order).\n- `op_id = hex(sha256(canonical_bytes))`. Full 64-hex internally; a 12-hex short\n  form for display, mirroring the ticket short-id convention.\n- Content that feeds the hash MUST include everything that makes the op unique:\n  ticket id, op kind, field payload, author, Lamport value, and created-at. Two\n  genuinely distinct edits must not collide; an identical replayed op must.\n\n## Changes\n\n- New module `crates/ticgit-lib/src/oplog/hash.rs` (or `ops.rs`) exposing\n  `fn content_id(bytes: &[u8]) -> String` and a typed `OpId`.\n- Add `sha2` to `ticgit-lib` deps (check the `gix` stack for a compatible version;\n  `gix` already pulls a sha backend — prefer reusing it over a second impl).\n- `keys.rs`: no change yet (op key layout is owned by step 4), but reserve the\n  `ops:<lamport>:<hash>` shape in a doc comment so step 4 slots in cleanly.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Unit test: same payload → same id; one-byte change → different id.\n- Unit test: canonical encoding is stable across runs/process restarts (no map\n  ordering flakiness).\n- Short-id collisions are astronomically unlikely but display code must tolerate\n  them (fall back to longer prefix), mirroring `resolve_id`'s unique-prefix rule.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Hash-input drift: if step 4 later changes the op payload shape, ids change.\n  Mitigate by versioning the op payload (step 2) and freezing the canonical\n  encoding behind a documented function.","state":"review","status":"open","title":"Content-derived IDs (SHA-256 of op content)"}}}